x) are both fed into a 'Discriminator' (orange box), which outputs classifi=
cations 'Fake' and 'Real,' respectively.  The discriminator's output is use=
d to train both the generator and the discriminator. The bottom section, la=
beled 'GAN inference,' shows only the generator (green box) and the process=
 of generating an image ('Generated...') from random vectors ('Random ve...=
'). The discriminator (grey box with an 'X' through it) is absent, indicati=
ng that during inference, only the generator is used to produce new images;=
 the discriminator is not involved in the generation process.  Arrows indic=
ate the direction of data flow between components." loading=3D"lazy" width=
